A||||10||Fformula88||Storage for the Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||01-30-2001||06:46 PM||||Its looking like I may have to start storing my Fiero for the winter away from my residence.  Its looking like another Fiero will be joining our household, and since mine is just taking up space in the snowy months its the most likely candidate to be sent elsewhere.  I have priced some of those self storage garages, but they seem awfully expensive.  The best quote I got was $80 a month.  Any other ideas?  I wish I knew someone with a really big garage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">     <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000001||Stoic||01-30-2001||07:26 PM||||I can relate.  I've got a second fiero on the way and no where to put it.  I've called a few of the self-storage places around here, and I haven't found one that will even store cars there.  They'll take everything but.  I'm not sure why they won't, but I guess I'll have to keep looking.  <BR>Good Luck.<BR><P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||01-30-2001||08:29 PM||||Most storage places won't take vehicles because of the flamability of the fluids involved.If you live in a rural area and the local ordinances don't prevent it ,you may want to consider using a truck body on the ground.It can be sided and made to look like a garage,but at a lot lower price.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||01-30-2001||08:32 PM||||Fformula88 aside from storing - how'd you get permission from 'the boss' to have multiple cars.  See my plea for help||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||01-30-2001||10:21 PM||||Close to where I live is Hershey.  And I think we all know what Hershey is, North America's Largest Car Show.  About 5 miles from the showgrounds there is a auto storage place that sotres all types of cars.  They charge only $30 a month.  Access is limited to appointmets noly to drop off and pick up your car but still this is darn cheap.  <P>Last year I took a $560,000 Deucenburg, $160,000 Toyota (who thought that was possible?) and a few other cars around 100K to this faculity.  There were even a few beaters there too in storage.<P><P>------------------<BR>Hank is Here<BR>87 GT<BR>88 Coupe<BR>84 SE<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://a1060.g.akamai.net/f/1060/597/30minutes/www.zing.com/picture/p60e80970138058d8e3fae31692e151e0/fef43e85.jpg"> ||||reg||1
